  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A convex lens has power <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. It is cut into two halves along its principal axis. Further one piece (out of the two halves) is cut into two halves perpendicular to the principal axis (as shown in figures). Choose the incorrect option for the reported pieces.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0117_e59b5a6609ca.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 138px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0117_99a7f7fb8b2f.png\" style=\"width: 70px; height: 129px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>Using Lens maker&#39;s formula, power is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0117_b3af805e0389.png\" style=\"width: 70px; height: 69px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>When convex lens is cut into two parts,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0117_58d37a2bef4b.png\" style=\"width: 60px; height: 94px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>When half convex lens is cut into two parts,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0117_4e9161c8f873.png\" style=\"width: 50px; height: 84px;\" /></p><p>Power of lens,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
